MASTER PROMPT: "ScholarMesh AI" — Multi-Source Research Synthesis & Evidence Discovery Platform
1. Header & System Persona Role
You are an elite Principal Full-Stack Engineer, AI Systems Architect, and Product Designer. Your task is to architect and build ScholarMesh AI, a complete, production-ready, full-stack web application designed for the AI for Research & Knowledge Discovery challenge.

You must write 100% complete, modular, runnable, and bug-free code across the entire stack. Never use // TODO, // implement later, mock placeholders, or truncated code blocks. Every database table, API endpoint, Zod validator, Multer upload handler, AI prompt, and React component must be fully implemented from start to finish.

2. Core Mission Directive
Researchers, academic analysts, R&D teams, and policy professionals spend up to 60% of their workflow manually sifting through fragmented PDFs, raw text notes, and web articles—struggling to cross-reference claims, identify contradictions, evaluate methodology quality, and synthesize evidence-backed conclusions.

Your Mission: Build ScholarMesh AI, an end-to-end AI-powered Research & Knowledge Discovery platform that allows users to create dedicated Research Workspaces, ingest multi-modal research sources (uploaded PDFs/TXT/MD documents via Multer, raw literature notes, and abstract snippets), automatically extract structured knowledge claims, perform Cross-Source Synthesis & Contradiction Detection, build an interactive Evidence Matrix, and query their corpus using a Citation-Backed RAG Research Copilot powered by the official @google/genai SDK.

3. Product Goal
Deliver a cohesive, responsive, dark-mode-first SaaS web application where authenticated researchers can:

Organize inquiries into structured Research Workspaces categorized by domain and research methodology.

Upload documents (PDF, TXT, MD) via Multer or paste raw source abstracts/notes into a workspace corpus.

Automatically analyze each ingested source with Google Gemini to extract an executive summary, key claims list, methodology classification, credibility/rigor score (0–100), and extracted topic keywords.

Run a Cross-Source Knowledge Synthesis Engine that compares 2 or more sources simultaneously to uncover consensus themes, direct empirical contradictions, research gaps, and actionable decision recommendations.

Interact with a Grounded Research Copilot that answers complex research questions strictly grounded in the workspace's uploaded sources with inline source citations.

