7. User Flow
Onboarding: User registers an account or clicks "Use Demo Researcher Account" on /login -> receives JWT token -> redirected to /dashboard.

Workspace Creation: User clicks "New Research Workspace" -> inputs title (e.g., "mRNA Delivery Lipid Nanoparticles: Efficacy vs. Hepatic Toxicity"), domain (Biomedical & Clinical Sciences), primary research question, and working hypothesis -> saved to PostgreSQL.

Source Ingestion: Inside /workspaces/:id, user uploads 2–5 PDF/TXT research papers via Multer or pastes study abstracts (or clicks "Load Sample Study" to populate realistic papers immediately).

Automated AI Indexing: Backend extracts text from the file or body, invokes Gemini with a strict JSON Schema to generate an executive summary, methodology critique, rigor score (0–100), topic keywords, and atomic claims, then stores everything in sources and extracted_claims tables.

Knowledge Discovery & Synthesis: User navigates to Synthesis Studio, selects 2+ sources, chooses a synthesis lens (e.g., Systematic Literature Review or Contradiction & Bias Audit), and clicks "Run Cross-Source Synthesis".

Insight Inspection: Gemini compares all selected sources and returns a structured JSON report displaying Consensus Themes, Direct Contradictions between studies, Unanswered Research Gaps, and an Evidence-Based Decision Matrix.

Interactive Interrogation: User opens the Research Copilot tab and asks specific questions (e.g., "Where do these studies disagree on dosing thresholds and what sample sizes were used?"), receiving answers strictly grounded in the workspace corpus with source citations.

