10. Database Schema (Production SQL for PostgreSQL)
Create an automatic database initialization script (server/src/db/init.sql executed automatically on server startup) with the following production PostgreSQL schema:

SQL
CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS "uuid-ossp";

-- 1. Users Table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  full_name VARCHAR(120) NOT NULL,
  email VARCHAR(255) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
  password_hash TEXT NOT NULL,
  institution VARCHAR(180) DEFAULT 'Independent Research Institute',
  research_role VARCHAR(100) DEFAULT 'Principal Investigator',
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 2. Research Workspaces Table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS workspaces (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  title VARCHAR(200) NOT NULL,
  domain VARCHAR(60) NOT NULL,
  research_question TEXT NOT NULL,
  working_hypothesis TEXT,
  default_synthesis_mode VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'systematic_review',
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
  updated_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 3. Research Sources (Documents / Notes / Papers) Table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sources (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  workspace_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  title VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  authors VARCHAR(255) DEFAULT 'Unknown Authors',
  publication_year INT,
  source_type VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL DEFAULT 'peer_reviewed_paper',
  original_filename VARCHAR(255),
  raw_content TEXT NOT NULL,
  word_count INT DEFAULT 0,
  ai_summary TEXT,
  methodology_notes TEXT,
  rigor_score INT DEFAULT 0 CHECK (rigor_score >= 0 AND rigor_score <= 100),
  rigor_justification TEXT,
  key_topics JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 4. Extracted Atomic Claims & Evidence Table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS extracted_claims (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  source_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES sources(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  workspace_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  claim_text TEXT NOT NULL,
  claim_category VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  supporting_quote TEXT,
  confidence_level VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'high',
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 5. Cross-Source Synthesis Reports Table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS synthesis_reports (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  workspace_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  title VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,
  synthesis_mode VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,
  source_ids JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
  executive_summary TEXT NOT NULL,
  consensus_themes JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
  contradictions JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
  research_gaps JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
  decision_recommendations JSONB NOT NULL DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
  overall_evidence_strength VARCHAR(40) NOT NULL,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

-- 6. Workspace Copilot Chat Messages Table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS copilot_messages (
  id UUID PRIMARY KEY DEFAULT uuid_generate_v4(),
  workspace_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES workspaces(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  user_id UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES users(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
  role VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL CHECK (role IN ('user', 'assistant')),
  message_text TEXT NOT NULL,
  citations JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
  follow_up_questions JSONB DEFAULT '[]'::jsonb,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_workspaces_user ON workspaces(user_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_sources_workspace ON sources(workspace_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_claims_workspace ON extracted_claims(workspace_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_synthesis_workspace ON synthesis_reports(workspace_id);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_copilot_workspace ON copilot_messages(workspace_id);
11. Row Level Security (RLS) / Data Isolation Rules
Enforce strict tenant isolation across every SQL query and API handler:

Every protected route must extract req.user.id from the verified JWT payload (never trust user_id sent in request body or query params).

All SELECT, UPDATE, and DELETE queries on workspaces, sources, extracted_claims, synthesis_reports, and copilot_messages MUST include WHERE user_id = $1 (or verify workspace ownership first via SELECT id FROM workspaces WHERE id = $1 AND user_id = $2).

If a user attempts to access, modify, or synthesize a workspace or source ID belonging to another user, immediately return 404 Not Found or 403 Forbidden.

12. Backend API Routes
All routes are prefixed with /api:

Auth Routes (/api/auth)
POST /api/auth/register — Validate input with Zod, hash password with bcrypt (10 salt rounds), create user, return { token, user }.

POST /api/auth/login — Verify credentials, sign JWT (expiresIn: '7d'), return { token, user }.

GET /api/auth/me — Protected route returning current user profile and aggregate dashboard counts.

Workspace Routes (/api/workspaces)
GET /api/workspaces — List all workspaces for req.user.id (supports ?domain= and ?search= query filters) with dynamic counts of source_count, claim_count, and synthesis_count.

POST /api/workspaces — Validate with Zod and create a new research workspace.

GET /api/workspaces/:id — Get full workspace details, including its ingested sources, extracted claims count, and synthesis reports.

DELETE /api/workspaces/:id — Delete a workspace and cascade-delete associated records.

Source Ingestion & AI Analysis Routes (/api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sources)
POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sources — Supports multipart/form-data (via Multer single file field document up to 10MB for .pdf, .txt, .md) OR JSON body (raw_content, title, authors, publication_year, source_type).

Extracts text from the uploaded file buffer (pdf-parse for PDFs, buffer.toString('utf-8') for TXT/MD) or uses raw_content.

Calls Gemini analyzeSourceDocument() to extract ai_summary, methodology_notes, rigor_score, rigor_justification, key_topics, and extracted_claims.

Inserts the source into sources and bulk-inserts all extracted claims into extracted_claims inside a PostgreSQL transaction.

GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sources — List all ingested sources in the workspace ordered by created_at DESC.

DELETE /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/sources/:sourceId — Remove a source and its associated claims.

Claims Explorer Route (/api/workspaces/:workspaceId/claims)
GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/claims — Retrieve all extracted claims for a workspace joined with sources.title, sources.authors, and sources.rigor_score, filterable by ?category=, ?confidence=, and ?search=.

AI Cross-Source Synthesis Routes (/api/workspaces/:workspaceId/synthesize)
POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/synthesize — Accepts { source_ids: string[], synthesis_mode: string, title?: string }. Verifies at least 2 sources belong to the workspace, retrieves their summaries, metadata, and extracted claims, calls Gemini generateCrossSourceSynthesis(), saves the structured report to synthesis_reports, and returns the saved report.

GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/syntheses — List all synthesis reports for the workspace.

GET /api/syntheses — List all synthesis reports across all workspaces for the logged-in user.

Grounded Research Copilot Routes (/api/workspaces/:workspaceId/copilot)
GET /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/copilot — Fetch conversation history for the workspace.

POST /api/workspaces/:workspaceId/copilot — Accepts { question: string }. Retrieves all workspace sources & extracted claims as grounded context, calls Gemini askResearchCopilot(), saves both the user message and assistant response (with structured citations and follow-up prompts) in copilot_messages, and returns the response.

