18. Security Requirements
Password Security: Never store plaintext passwords. Always hash with bcryptjs (saltRounds = 10).

JWT Authentication: Sign tokens using process.env.JWT_SECRET and verify via an authenticateToken Express middleware on all protected /api/* routes.

File Upload Hardening: Configure Multer with limits: { fileSize: 10 * 1024 * 1024 } (10MB max) and a fileFilter allowing only .pdf, .txt, and .md files.

Input Sanitization & Validation: Validate all request bodies with Zod before executing database queries or Gemini API calls. Return structured 400 Bad Request JSON with clear error messages.

Rate Limiting & Headers: Apply helmet() and express-rate-limit (150 requests per 15 minutes on general API routes, 30 requests per 15 minutes on AI generation routes).

